WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:05.529
Sylvester Stallone is pumped to be playing
John J. Rambo one last time, and that excitement

00:00:05.529 --> 00:00:08.040
seems to be fueled by some new creative energy.

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:12.900
As he's done several times in recent months,
the star took to Instagram to share new images

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:17.540
and backstory text for his upcoming movie,
giving us a deeper insight into the iconic

00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:21.460
character whose story he'll be closing out
with Rambo V: Last Blood.

00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:27.350
Introduced in 1982's First Blood, Rambo was
never given much of a detailed history beyond

00:00:27.350 --> 00:00:30.680
being a Green Beret, who, as you know, are
real badasses.

00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:35.059
At the time, the fact that he was trained
to ignore pain, live off the land, and eat

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:38.900
things that would make a billy goat puke was
all the backstory that we needed.

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:44.059
But Sly's latest post, depicting the one-man
army as a fresh-faced young man not yet molded

00:00:44.059 --> 00:00:48.920
into the ultimate killing machine, contained
some surprisingly specific details about Rambo's

00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:50.020
time in the military.

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:55.079
It also alluded to the idea that for him,
war is more of a constant state of mind than

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:56.000
anything else.

00:00:56.200 --> 00:01:01.030
A second photo, most likely taken on-set of
the movie, shows Sly in character as he's

00:01:01.030 --> 00:01:05.100
either nursing a serious headache or about
to kill somebody, perhaps both.

00:01:05.409 --> 00:01:10.340
The saga of Rambo was one of the more reliable
action franchises of the '80s, despite the

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:13.560
fact that First Blood was never intended to
launch a series.

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:18.820
The first flick was adapted from a novel of
the same name by David Morrell, in which a

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:23.620
mysterious, traumatized Vietnam vet is pursued
by police through the forests of the Northwest.

00:01:23.869 --> 00:01:28.440
He's being chased down for the petty crime
of vagrancy, and the pursuit does not end

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:29.440
well for the police.

00:01:29.729 --> 00:01:34.380
In the novel, Rambo ends the story by taking
his own life, a fate which was almost shared

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:35.640
by the character in the movie.

00:01:35.890 --> 00:01:40.580
In fact, Stallone had to talk First Blood
director Ted Kotcheff into cutting poor Rambo

00:01:40.580 --> 00:01:44.320
a break, altering the ending after the original
scene had been shot.

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:48.220
Although the film got mixed reviews, it cleaned
up at the box office.

00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:54.049
For the sequel, 1985's Rambo: First Blood
Part II, the character transitioned from put-upon

00:01:54.049 --> 00:01:56.560
anti-hero to full-on agent of death.

00:01:56.860 --> 00:02:01.299
The follow-up saw Rambo returning to Vietnam
on a fact-finding mission, which eventually

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:06.500
evolved into a 1-versus-everyone gunfight
that seemed to involve the entire country.

00:02:06.740 --> 00:02:11.280
That film also put up numbers at the box office,
rendering the name "Rambo" as shorthand for

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:13.860
"badass" for the rest of the decade and beyond.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:15.300
"He thinks he's Rambo."

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:19.200
"Rambo is a p----."

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:26.220
1988's Rambo III moved the action to Afghanistan,
and seemingly served as an end to the series...

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:27.520
until 2008.

00:02:27.830 --> 00:02:33.120
Two decades after Rambo III, Stallone returned
to work both sides of the camera in the simply-titled

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:33.780
Rambo.

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:38.490
The fourth movie saw our hero laying low,
minding his own business as a snake catcher

00:02:38.490 --> 00:02:42.550
in Thailand before being forced back into
action to protect a group of missionaries

00:02:42.550 --> 00:02:44.280
from corrupt Burmese soldiers.

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:48.880
While the movie's reviews were mixed, franchise
fans mostly found it to be a satisfactory

00:02:48.890 --> 00:02:54.750
continuation of Rambo's story and were also
blown away by its insane level of bloody violence.

00:02:54.750 --> 00:02:59.920
Now comes Rambo V. Throughout the production
of the series' final installment, Stallone

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:03.620
has popped up on Instagram to share set photos
that help sketch out the story.

00:03:04.010 --> 00:03:08.940
Among those photos is a cowboy hat-sporting
Rambo looking intense in a rainstorm, another

00:03:08.950 --> 00:03:13.320
with him riding a horse, an image of Rambo
and his bow and arrow, and a short series

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:15.180
highlighting the film's co-stars.

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:19.360
Helping to fill in some more details is the
movie's official synopsis, which helps to

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:21.040
explain the cowboy hat.

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:25.760
According to the summary, Rambo V will see
John Rambo living and working on a ranch in

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:26.480
Arizona.

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:28.640
But this is no pastoral life.

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:33.700
John's violent past has left him feeling deeply
troubled, suffering from PTSD.

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:37.920
When a longtime family friend informs him
that her granddaughter has gone missing in

00:03:37.930 --> 00:03:40.900
Mexico, he sets off with her to locate the
young woman.

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:45.370
The journey leads him to uncover a ring of
sex-traffickers and kidnappers, led by a vicious

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:48.060
crime lord whom he must stop at all costs.

00:03:48.350 --> 00:03:52.720
As we all know, being deeply troubled and
traumatized by combat has never kept Rambo

00:03:52.730 --> 00:03:56.900
from bringing the pain in the past, and we
don't see any reason why this final outing

00:03:56.900 --> 00:03:57.920
will be any different.

00:03:58.120 --> 00:04:02.560
While no release date has been announced,
Rambo V is expected to hit screens sometime

00:04:02.570 --> 00:04:07.190
in 2019, but just because it's the end of
the line for the Vietnam vet doesn't mean

00:04:07.190 --> 00:04:09.500
it won't be fun to watch him draw Last Blood.

00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:12.860
"It sounds like it's very depressing, but
it's not.

00:04:12.860 --> 00:04:14.380
It's a kids' film!"

